    {
      "id": "claim_c75cf7d32aa248b48eb6f343c98b8715",
      "statement": "GitHub Pages is purely static hosting and cannot set custom response headers (no `_headers` file, no per-response config). This is currently fine because CheerpJ 4.x does not require cross-origin isolation (COOP/COEP) or SharedArrayBuffer; its stated server requirements are HTTPS plus HTTP Range-request support, both of which GitHub Pages provides.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L108-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0bf5cbb97fe72008146a4f611fb9654cc7891e38effb6d0d1bf2bc2618ae49b2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L353-L362",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01225f6f252b289b91bcd885b27aa11cc3696978e9d57d9d74fb524f03acc63f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6fd69666f9744f1caac6377425a00bc3",
      "statement": "If a future engine upgrade ever required cross-origin isolation (e.g. for SharedArrayBuffer/WASM threads), GitHub Pages could not satisfy it directly; the documented workaround is coi-serviceworker, a client-side service worker that injects COOP/COEP headers on a host that cannot set them itself. It is not needed today and is noted as a forward-compatibility escape hatch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L108-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0bf5cbb97fe72008146a4f611fb9654cc7891e38effb6d0d1bf2bc2618ae49b2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L362-L375",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53c375a0dc6396da5ce6fbd9f9a1f033ffe816a59f7e89ec50d032b9199a4511:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95946f2fd1fd49d2a3fe39b130f4be55",
      "statement": "CheerpJ 4.x has full production-ready support for Java 8 and Java 11 (partial/production-supported Java 17). Kata templates and reference solutions target Java 8/11 features and must avoid Java 17-only syntax (records, sealed classes, pattern-matching switch). This is a content-authoring rule on `katas/*.md`, not a build flag, because Java is compiled at runtime in the browser by CheerpJ's in-browser javac rather than during `npm run build`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L116-L119",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8e115474a1e606afe688bc6ab302c1c3c718c477ca054427cb785ad01719700:"
