        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a181e45bb2bf4da499e6fa596fcf5650",
      "statement": "The runner always tears down and rebuilds the sandbox iframe after each run (on result, timeout, or Stop) rather than reusing the CheerpJ session, to avoid the JVM classloader serving a stale `Main`/`KataRunner` class from a previous run under the same class names. A fresh iframe is created lazily on the next run. Stop hard-kills via `worker.terminate()` inside the relay and resolves the pending promise as `{status:'stopped'}`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://public/sandbox.js#L18-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5846d0f3ce436ccea3859701adb20c0250beac6455b9e8d14f2d1b0b36ee2cd6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/runner/runner.ts#L50-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42ade35912c03f633711a47274717872a1ffdf3d0a40bb7a3fe80422a237904b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/runner/runner.ts#L83-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c230973a71f35226f784989fd7c2ea934a9ab7ab414ba0b8bc91c5d11e695a5d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b92c9590a93d43fc9c56a4d3f78af0fc",
      "statement": "CheerpJ runs inside a dedicated Worker (not the sandbox iframe's main thread) specifically so a tight non-yielding infinite loop in learner Java (e.g. `while(true){}`) cannot wedge the thread that owns the run timeout. The iframe's `sandbox.js` stays responsive, its setTimeout fires on timeout, and `worker.terminate()` hard-kills the runaway code from outside regardless of what it is doing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L102-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c113752c5305d0399dd0bad7647b83926d246ea877ae1c7226e45e9d35084ca:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://public/sandbox-worker.js#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23efec9aea6ce960efaae8c138b1ec25bbceb3387ca818be7927f3b92f5d12a3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://public/sandbox.js#L1-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d18e61b934fb4d735e9584fb82885b592e1f116c23a81f9bf8b7d8653b20673:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_794fc0d2373c43e99081cceea675baa9",
      "statement": "Inside the Worker there is no DOM, so CheerpJ's stdout/stderr land on the Worker's own `console.log`/`console.error`. `sandbox-worker.js` intercepts `log`/`error`/`warn`/`info` for the duration of each run to capture that text, then parses sentinel-delimited stdout (`___KATA_OUT_BEGIN___`/`___KATA_OUT_END___`) and `___KATA_RET___` lines back out into a `RunResult` posted up through the iframe to the main thread.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://public/sandbox-worker.js#L16-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:daa9033b641378ea53427ed989726a1edea3519539d8fd5836adfd37d4b75c91:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://public/sandbox-worker.js#L62-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7407ed08c6c1572fb0c6e0247fa85fa80e2576d7008806a974a986ebada438ab:"
        }
      ]
